Capitol: Themyscira
Location: Continent around 40N
Population: ~17,000

   The primary colony and capitol of Pandora, Themyscira, is composed of two separate sub-colonies linked to one another through a transportation network that allows fast & easy movement between the two. The older, more developed by less inhabited Island of Aeaea, serves as a terraformed safe zone for the human population of the planet and sits at the moth of Kybelle Bay. The City of Themyscira is the newer, less developed sub-colony and serves as the technological, industrial, and military heart of the colony. Linking the two sub-colonies are a number of ferries that travel over the bay, and a monorail that goes around the bay.

KYBELLE BAY
   Kybele Bay is a massive, kidney-shaped basin stretching 75 miles from its northern reaches to its southern curve. To the southwest and northeast, the bay tapers into elegant, funnel-like channels. These narrowing waterways act as natural accelerators for the brackish water as it transitions into the major river systems feeding the basin.
   Spanning 52 miles at its widest point, the interior of the bay is a tranquil, sun-drenched expanse. Because the basin rarely exceeds 200 feet in depth, the tropical sun penetrates nearly to the floor, turning the water into a brilliant spectrum of cyan and emerald. Just past the artificial white glass-sand of the beach, vast Seagrass Meadows sway in the tidal currents. From the surface, these look like undulating fields of neon green, swaying in sync with the pulse of the bay. As the floor slopes toward the center, the grass gives way to towering Kelp Forests. These massive, amber-hued stalks reach up from the darkness like cathedral columns, their canopies occasionally breaking the surface during low tide. t its deepest points—a wide trench carved by the ancient flow between the two inlets—the water turns a bruised, deep navy, hiding the dangerous aquatic predators that prowl the kelp-line. 
   Just above the high-tide mark, the sand gives way to a twenty-yard band of polished basalt cobbles. These dark, charcoal-grey stones have been tumbled smooth by colonial machinery and laid in a dense, shifting layer that clacks loudly under the weight of any encroaching predator, serving as a primitive but effective acoustic alarm. At the water’s edge, the beach of the bay is made of an artificial white glass-sand. This crystalline grit, reclaimed from the bay's own floor, stays blindingly white even under the tropical sun, reflecting the turquoise light of the shallow seagrass meadows. Beyond the stones, a mile-wide buffer of genetically-stiffened bamboo towering sixty feet high is planted in precise, airy rows that allow security drones and sentries a clear line of sight while creating an underground mat of rhizomes that no native flora can penetrate.
   The bay’s mouth on the eastern side is guarded by a 16-mile-long central island, a narrow sliver of land only 1.5 to 3 miles wide. It is flanked by two reaching peninsulas—24 miles to the north and 18 miles to the south—creating two distinct, narrow inlets, each only 2–3 miles wide. The island serves as the colony’s most secure sanctuary; all local wildlife has been systematically eradicated and replaced with familiar Terran flora and fauna. This artificial paradise is home to approximately 5,000 inhabitants: 1,200 mostly older citizens, supported by 230 slaves and a population of 3,600 children, all living within the safest environment for humans on the planet.
   Commanding the bay's western coastline is the colony's first major terrestrial expansion, a new city. This vast project, a geometric "double ring," is not just a settlement; it is a declaration of intent, engineered to establish the same level of absolute control on the main continent that exists on the central island. The city is critically situated between two powerful, freshwater river deltas. From the air, it resembles a geometric "eye" set within the natural "V" formed by the two converging waterways. The larger outer ring of the city, 14 miles in diameter, has large agricultural areas occupying around 1/5th of the mostly empty area. The smaller, inner ring is 1.4 miles in diameter and holds the actual developing city. At the absolute center of this vast industrial circle sits the inner ring. Only 1.4 miles in diameter, this dense, vertically-oriented hub holds the developing city proper.

THE ISLAND OF AEAEA
   The 16-mile-long island is a curated masterpiece of Terran ecology. Spanning 28 square miles, the island is a meticulously maintained masterwork of Terran biology. The aggressive, high-oxygen flora of the mainland has been entirely purged, replaced by a Tropical Garden Paradise. The landscape is a vibrant tapestry of Earth-standard palms, flowering hibiscus, and sprawling banyan trees. Manicured botanical gardens and orchid-lined walking paths wind between the estates, maintained with a precision that makes the island feel more like a high-end resort than a frontier settlement. The most scenic coastal ridges and elevated plateaus are claimed by the Twelve Ruling Houses. These massive estates are designed with open-air architecture to catch the bay breezes, surrounded by private groves of fruit-bearing Terran trees like mango, citrus, and coconut. Interspersed among these are the quieter, luxury enclaves housing the 1,178 Free Adults—mostly retired or semi-retired colonists who have traded the industrial grind of the mainland for a life of "civilized" tropical leisure. A significant portion of the island’s interior is dedicated to several large boarding school campuses. These institutions house and educate the 3,677 children of the colony. The schools are designed as "living classrooms," where the students grow up surrounded by the safety of Earth’s biology, largely shielded from the reality of the predatory world just across the water. The western, leeward side of the island is home to extensive docking facilities. While private slips house the yachts of the Twelve Houses, a steady fleet of ferries traverses the 52-mile expanse, across the bay to the new city.

TRANSPORTATION
   Following the gentle curve of the southern coastline, the high-speed Maglev monorail serves as the primary land-link between the Central Island and the mainland expansion. The track covers a total distance of 135 miles—winding along the inner edge of the engineered shoreline—and completes the transit in a mere 25 minutes. At these sustained high velocities, the Maglev represents the pinnacle of the colony’s transportation network, far outstripping the hour-long ferry crossing. While the Maglev handles the bulk of the colony's transit, the elite utilize personal VTOLs, such as the sleek Altovolo Sigma. These high-performance craft allow the them to hop directly from their island homes to the Inner Ring of the new city in minutes.

THE CITY OF THEMYSCIRA
   The city's outer boundary is a 10m (33 ft) tall rampart of reinforced plascrete, 0.46m (1.5ft) thick. This wall forms a 70km (44-mile) circuit, standing as the definitive line between the curated agricultural zones and the wild delta. The wall is a continuous weapon platform, utilizing a tiered hierarchy of surveillance and firepower:
* Weapon Emplacements (Every 150m): 2m diameter hardened nodes housing automated plasma cannons and high-velocity flamethrowers. In the high-oxygen atmosphere, the flamethrowers are devastatingly effective, creating intense, long-reaching thermal barriers to incinerate encroaching flora or biomass.
* Guard Towers (Every 450m): 3m diameter elevated towers that serve as the primary sensor nodes. These house the localized AI sub-processors that manage the weapons and drones dedicated to defending that section of the wall.
* Guard Stations (Every 1,800m): Thirty reinforced command hubs, each garrisoned by a squad of soldiers. These humans serve as the fail-safe for the AI controlled defenses, overseeing the automated systems and drone swarms in their 1.8km sector.
* At eight strategic intervals, separated by 7,200m, the wall is punctuated by Airlock Forts. These large, bunker style complexes manage all ground traffic into the city. Each fort is garrisoned by a full platoon of soldiers, providing a heavy rapid-response force in addition to ensuring no hostile flora make it into the city through the gates. On the other side of those gates is a 100m dead zone and then the Pandoran jungle.
   Within the outer walls lies a 400 sq kilometer region surrounding the smaller inner zone. Ten large farms are found in different areas within the outer zone, each of which has around 350 slaves housed in a prison-like complex at the farms heart to work the farm. Another farm with a more relaxed setting and easier to farm crops houses soon-to-be mothers, women that have recently given birth, and a cadre of elder slaves that care for the 4,681 slave children. All slaves more than 3 years old are fitted with 'control collars' that include sophisticated biomonitors, sensors, and behavior modifying tools to help control the slave population using AI overseers. Almost every aspect of a slaves life is overseen and controlled by AI, with human overseers plus a platoon of soldiers in case of an emergency stationed in a control building within each farm complex. The slaves are housed in 5 person communal dorm-rooms that each have 4 single person bunks and 1 double person bed. These rooms are assigned by the controlling AI and those assigned to a specific room are rotated randomly on a weekly basis. In addition, there are a number of private rooms available that are assigned for one night to individuals as a reward along with one person of their choosing. Like a modern prison, the farm housing complex also includes a number of recreational facilities, a kitchen, laundry, etc for everyday life. Everything a slave does is monitored and evaluated by the controlling AI within the housing complex, which is specifically looking for behavior patterns. The human overseers and soldiers very rarely interact with the slaves directly.
   In addition to the 11 farms, there are a number of military installations and the starport with an adjoining airfield. within the outer zone. Each of the military installations are designed like small military bases with a command building, a motor pool, a mess hall, and several barracks buildings. While each military installation looks to be designed for a battalion, they currently only have around a company each. The starport, usually has 1-3 dropships and several small transports on landing pads but has room for up 12 dropships and 20 smaller transports ay a single time. The adjoining airfield has multiple fighter craft, cargo transports, and heavy lift haulers coming and going at all times. The starport and adjoining airfield take up around 1/10th of the mostly empty area in the outer zone.
   The colonies monorail passes over the outer wall in the southwest, adjacent an extra large Airlock Fort, and stops for a short period at a monorail terminal, before making a curved, almost spiral approach to the inner zone.
   Within the outermost zone lies the much smaller 4 sq km inner zone, which is also protected by another 10m (33 ft) tall rampart of reinforced plascrete, 0.46m (1.5ft) thick. Like the outer wall, the inner wall is a nearly continuous weapons platform that utilizes a tiered hierarchy of surveillance and firepower: 
* Guard Towers (Every 100m): 4m diameter multi-role nodes. Each integrates automated plasma cannons, high-velocity flamethrowers, anti-aircraft lasers, and plasma point-defense systems. They serve as both electronic sensor hubs and squad-capable strongpoints.
* Sentry Stations (Every 400m): 32m diameter mini-fortresses with 1m thick walls. These serve as command-and-control centers equipped with anti-aircraft missile systems and housing for a full platoon. (Status: 4 of 18 completed).
* Sentry Fortress: At 6 locations, 60 degrees (1200m) apart from one another, at the end of one of the major spokes of the inner city are 6 large bunker-airlocks. These large, bunker style complexes manage all ground traffic into the city, can house a full company of soldiers, and has the ability to act as strategic command & control centers in the case of invasion. In addition to enough firepower to engage multiple large threats at once, the sentry fortress also has railguns that are able to engage ships in orbit. While all 6 sentry fortresses are operational, none of them are yet completed.
   Within the inner wall is a largely empty area that has fully built infrastructure for future development. The city is divided horizontally by 6 main spokes, which are 30m (100ft) wide thoroughfares and wide, open-air corridors that serve as the primary transit and utility infrastructure for the city core. Each of these spokes consist of integrated walkways, paved roadways for electric transport, and designated planting strips for local (harmless) flora. The basic power, water, and data infrastructure is embedded directly beneath these open-air corridors to support future expansion. These spokes serve as the centers or hearts of 6 districts, including:
* The Military District: When finished this district will have military family housing, off-duty housing, armories, firing ranges, drone hangers, vehicle maintenance shops, and various unit headquarters. At the moment there are only a few pre-fab buildings within each ring of the zone. The military district connects directly to the starport in the outer zone.
* Utilities District: When finished this district will have massive battery centers, fusion generators, water treatment facilities, desalination plants, and housing for utility workers.
* Manufacturing District: This district is the most developed at the moment, with a large number of pre-fab manufacturing centers (mostly devoted to construction), housing, and a number of small businesses selling manufactured consumer items. When finished it will be the home of all types of manufacturing in the city plus housing for the districts many workers, and many manufacturing related small businesses.
* Research District: Currently the second most developed district in the city, with a good number of prefab research centers, modular housing, and even a couple of coffee shops. When finished the district will have dozens of research centers, housing for scientists & engineers, and the colonies primary super computer.
* Healthcare District: Currently one of the least developed districts in the city, the healthcare district has a single pre-fab hospital, some pre-fab specialist centers, housing for the healthcare workers within the district, and a fully built fitness center.
* Education District: At present very little has been built in the education district other than a few training centers used by workers in other districts for training meetings and such. Eventually the district will house Elementary Schools, a High School, specialized tech schools, dorm buildings, housing, and more but for the moment all of that is handled on the island.
   The city is further divided by 7 concentric rings, centered on major ring-like concentric throughfares. These throughfares are only 15m (50ft) wide but are otherwise similar to the spokes in form & function. Each of the rings are dedicated to a specific function, and from the outermost ring inward are:
* The Transportation & Logistics Ring: Lying just within the inner zones wall, and separated from it by 30m (100ft), this ring will have all the cities transport services, vehicle services, and warehouses. At present only the military, manufacturing, utilities, and research districts have anything developed in this area with the manufacturing district having the most development.
* The Heavy Industry Ring (~6.1km circumference): When fully developed this ring will have a districts primary or largest buildings such as the medical center in the Healthcare District or the main Command Headquarters in the Military District. At the moment only the Manufacturing District as any significant development in this area, with multiple large industrial & construction grade fabrication centers. Within the Utilities District there is some development also with a large water treatment facility and the cities only fusion power plant.
* The Light Industry Ring (~5.2km circumference): When the city has been fully developed this ring will have all the secondary & peripheral industries related to the district within it. This means smaller specialized schools in the Education District, Tech startups in the Research District, and specialized military department offices in the Military District as an example. At present most of the 'industry' within each of the districts is located in this area so that larger facilities can be built when they need to be in the Heavy Industry ring.
* The Housing Ring (~4.3km circumference): While the concept art and development plans shown in the Halls of the Founding Matrons might show terraced gardens, fountains, and beautiful high-tech high-rises for the future of this ring, the modern reality is large pre-fab apartment buildings and a few small parks. While individual apartments might be quite nice on the interior, the overall aesthetic is more akin to old soviet union style housing than ultra-modern utopia.
* The Shopping & Entertainment Ring (~3.5km circumference): In the future this ring will have shops, offices, music venues, holovid theatres, and more. At the moment this ring is almost totally empty, with most of the shopping & entertainment being located on the Government Ring.
* The Finance & Business Ring (~2.6km circumference): What will be the future Wall Street of Themyscira is a virtual ghost town at the moment other than a few small buildings in the Manufacturing District. For the moment Matron Olivia Allen and her small band of Financial wizards do what they can to organize & plan the economy from her home & offices in the capitol.
* Administrative Ring (~1.7km circumference): In a few decades this ring will be home most of the offices necessary for a functional government, including the courthouse, but at the moment it serves as the temporary shopping & entertainment section of the city. As the smallest and most compact ring it allows the current population of around 4,000 a place to gather & socialize without feeling they live in a ghost town. On the outer section of this ring are a large number of shops, bars, clubs, and more sit side-by-side one another in a mostly filled in ring. On the inside is the City Center, which is the most finished looking area in the city.
* City Center: The city center is an around 520m circular area holding more than 200,000 square meters (or around 50 acres) of land. Most of the city center looks like huge park with ponds, small forests, grassy areas, sports parks, and gravel walkways. Nestled among the sculpted hills & small forests in the city center are 6 large stone buildings that serve as the headquarters to the 6 ministries, as well as the personal homes of the 12 Founding Matrons. At the very center of this large park is the seat of Pandora's government, the Astraea, is a massive, tiered circular structure that serves as the physical and metaphorical axis of the city. Unlike the modular prefab units of the outer rings, it is constructed from reinforced white stone and high-tensile composites designed to last for centuries. This large building is built in a series of receding rings, each overflowing with meticulously maintained Terran gardens where the vines and broad-leafed trees grow with a prehistoric density, draping the white stone in a "living skin." At the heart of the tiers, a central column rises—housing the high-security council chambers of the 12 Founding Matrons and the primary uplink to the colony’s orbital assets. While most of the colonies administrative offices will eventually be located in the Administrative Ring, almost all of them are located within the Astraea at this time.
   Under the city, linking the various monorail stations to many points in the city, is a maze of tunnels that allow citizens to commute on AET's, which are like modern electric hoverboards. The AET's can be summoned and controlled through a citizens personal commlink, which allows a person arriving on the monorail to have one waiting for them by the time they ride the elevator down to the underground tunnel and then zips them to the closest exit near their destination. In the outer sections of these same tunnels are the utilities that give the city its water, power, and communication infrastructure.

MINISTRIES
Each of the Ministry buildings are virtually identical to one another on the exterior and very similar on the interior. Each floor of the building spans around 20,000 square feet and has space for 80-130 people to work. All the ministry building have three above ground stories and two below, but only the Ministry of Economics has developed the second floor, and none have developed the third.

